 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Wind for «ضل عنهم» (their gods vanish). 23 is Paradise: light mood and a light plate only (leaves before «ربهم»), no garden or river. Two paths for the two parties (24:2-6); the parable of the blind and the seeing is not drawn. STAGING v4: c1 (21-22: their loss in the Hereafter) is kept ambient. c2 (23-24) is staged in a plain town by day: three believers on the left (those who believed and did good deeds) stand in prayer on 23:3, bow on 23:4 (did good deeds) and prostrate on 23:6 (humbled before their Lord, As-Sa'di), and stand up on 23:9, before Paradise is named; Paradise is never drawn: only a light plate (23:10-14), no garden, river or gold. On 24:1 the other party, three faceless men in dark robes, comes in on the right (nobody stands there while the believers prostrate). The parable of the two parties: the deniers turn away on 24:3 (Al-Muyassar: they do not see the truth nor hear the caller), the camera goes to the believers for the seeing and hearing (24:5), and a two_paths plate for are they equal (24:7). The blind and deaf are not drawn literally. The cover now shows both parties (24:2)."
 },
